;; Temperature 0 is deduction, from Domingos, Tensor Logic, section 5.
;;
;; Parent(Alice, Bob) and Parent(Bob, Charlie) are the only facts.
;; The ancestor rule derives Ancestor(Alice, Charlie). It does not invent
;; Parent(Alice, Charlie), and it does not copy the entailment onto Dana
;; even though Dana's embedding is close to Charlie.
;; Raising T lets Dana borrow Charlie's entailment. Setting T back to 0
;; shuts that borrow off.
;;
;; Run:  cd go/arli && go run . ../../examples/zero-temp.arli

demo-zero-temp
